  "decision_summary": "Predicted pass: thiotepa is a small, neutral, low-TPSA phosphorothioamide with three aziridines. The most transferable evidence, AZQ, shows that aziridine-containing small molecules can achieve meaningful CSF/brain exposure after IV dosing. Poor-penetration comparators are largely ionizable, hydrophilic, or very large polar chelators, features absent in the query, so no strong contradictory evidence transfers.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct brain/CSF measurement for thiotepa itself is present in the supplied evidence.",
    "Morgan similarities to all evidence molecules are low, limiting quantitative transferability.",
    "Aziridine reactivity and potential rapid metabolism or covalent binding could alter in vivo CNS exposure."
  ],
